---
{% comment %}

There are problems outputting the proper JSON for a complex family:
1. This visualization assumes all people have only one partner
2. When things get messy immediately, i.e. Pierre dit St Malo has two marriages, the tree breaks down
3. The visualization assumes all children flow through the male

Therefore, as painful as it might be, we are relying on a hand-curated JSON file for the family tree

{% endcomment %}
---
{%- assign all_people = site.people -%}
{%- assign ignore = "1654-marie-m-nachita" -%}
[
{% for person in all_people %}
{%- unless ignore contains person.slug -%}
  {%- assign kids = site.people | where: "father", person.slug -%}
  {
    "id": "{{ person.slug }}",
    "name": "{{ person.name }}",
    "birth": "{{ person.born.date | date: "%Y" }}",
    "death": "{{ person.death.date | date: "%Y" }}",
    "spouse": "{{ person.partners[0].spouse }}",
    "parents": [ "{{ person.father }}", "{{ person.mother }}" ],{% if kids.size > 0 %}
    "children": [ {% for kid in kids %}"{{ kid.slug }}"{% unless forloop.last %}, {% endunless %}{% endfor %} ],{% endif %}
    "photo": "/path/to/image.jpg"
  }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
{%- endunless -%}
{% endfor %}
]